  ],
  "text": "You do not use ten percent of your brain. You use all of it, including while asleep. It is one of the most repeated wrong things anyone has ever said about you. Scan a brain doing almost nothing and there is activity right across the whole thing. There is no silent region waiting to be unlocked. Damage anywhere costs you something. But the real argument was never the scanning. It is the cost. Your brain is two percent of your body weight. It burns about twenty percent of your energy, every hour, awake or not. Nothing that expensive survives evolution while sitting idle. A body that could switch off nine tenths of that would have done it long ago. You are not idling at ten percent. You are running flat out, and it is costing you. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
